  The article says the gang attacked Kumar and tried to stab him, but the reel_script and caption call it an attempted murder ('கொலை முயற்சி') headline; the article's charge is attempted murder, so this matches, but the tamil_headline and slides_spec say the attack happened 'because of honking' (ஹாரன் அடித்ததால), which the article does not state as the cause; it only says Kumar honked and the group then abused and attacked him.
  The reel_script says Kumar was 'ஆடு மேய்க்கும் தொழிலாளி' and the article says the same, but the reel_script says the incident occurred 'near Kuppur' while the article places it near the Ayyanarappan temple in Kuppur, which is consistent; however the slides_spec sentence 'குமார் பைக்கில் தாராபுரம் செல்லும்போது நடந்தது' is fine, but the slide line 'சாலையில் மது அருந்தியவர்களிடம் குமார் ஹாரன் அடித்தார்' states the cause as honking without the article's sequence.
  The reel_script states the case was registered 'in 4 sections' and that 'two people were arrested yesterday', which matches the article, but the reel_script omits that the complaint was based on Kumar's complaint (it does mention the complaint), so no omission there.
  The caption says the group was 'ஆத்திரமடைந்த' (enraged) by the honking, an emotional motive not stated in the article.
